<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/7th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battle of the Trent</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/679">679</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/7th-century">7th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battle of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/trento">Trent</a> was fought in 679 near the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/river-trent">River Trent</a> between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aethelred-of-mercia">Æthelred of Mercia</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ecgfrith-of-northumbria">Ecgfrith of Northumbria</a>. Ælfwine, Ecgfrith's young brother, was killed, and Archbishop Theodore of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/canterbury">Canterbury</a> negotiated a peace in which Æthelred paid compensation for his death. The battle ended Northumbrian rule south of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/humber">Humber</a>, leaving Lindsey permanently Mercian.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-the-trent.jpg" alt="Battle of the Trent" width="320" height="333" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: myself · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Northumbria.rise.600.700.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
